{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1350259-the-tellurians-an-update","id":1350259,"title":"The Tellurians, an update.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-22T10:48:07-08:00","id":1350259,"title":"The Tellurians, an update.","content":"I think I started a topic similar to this some time ago, but I can't find it, and there was never a final written form. So here it is now. It should be noted that this legacy takes advantage of a quirk in the Nimbus rules which never makes it explicit how large an area can be marked by the Nimbus to get around considerations of AoE Scale. Still, I would recommend that if your player tries to claim that the world is a place, or something similar, that you blap them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gufIYdFkh3j136fVSSIzzza3fZd9NPmcZp6a5NRYkkc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Tellurians are a legacy that draws from several sources of mythology, those that have featured places of power, those that speak of the promised lands, and those that tie the ruler of a land to the health of that land and vice versa. They purport that they have existed for as long as humanity has been staking claims.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Origins: Obrimos, Seers, Silver Ladder.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Background: Many Claimers come from backgrounds that study or make use of claims of ownership over a place either via inheritance or right of rulership. Acquisitive real estate developers, historical landmark preservationists, people who claim descent from nobility, and holy pilgrims all find a place under this legacy\u2019s aegis. They seek to bind themselves to those things that are important to them, drawing power from their right to rule.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Appearance: Most Tellurians dress well, as befits kings, or those willing to make an impression of their connection to something important. Others opt simply for tokens of their self-claimed offices, or for garb that matches the locales they\u2019ve aligned themselves with.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Doctrine:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Space 2, Politics 2, and one of the following skills at 2 or higher: Occult, Survival, Streetwise.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiation: The prospective Tellurian must mark a place with his Nimbus, offering a challenge to take it by force, negotiation or any other method from anyone else who might lay a claim to it. Many find a place out of the way or with no other claimants, but some set themselves to truly epic challenges.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Organization: Hierarchy in the legacy is determined by achievement of attainments to some extent, but even more importantly by the number and impressiveness of the Claimer\u2019s holdings. Claimers will meet once a year at the holding of a particularly celebrated member where they will trade anything from notes to holdings. Sometimes more than one of them will work together in an area to acquire control over particularly large pieces of territory that they will then rule as a council of kings.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Theory: By laying a claim to something via their Nimbus the Tellurian establishes themselves as the link between their holding and the Supernal. Slowly this brings the world closer to the Supernal, and theoretically it\u2019s restoration to something akin to the Time Before. It also leashes the Supernal definitions and power of the Supernal from the holding to the King allowing them to draw power from it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Magic: Ruling Arcanum: Space</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras: Succeeding on a roll to assert their authority over their holding +2, Investigating the Mysteries of their holdings +1, Performing a survey, learning the history of, performing restoration on, protecting, or otherwise being a responsible King over their holding +2.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations: Time spent interacting with their holdings in a meaningful or beneficial way. Seeking out new places to lay a claim to.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainments</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First: The Survey</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Tellurian needs to be able to survey his realm to monitor its health and to be able to keep a sharp eye out for new opportunities to expand his holdings. This attainment mimics the Inward and Outward Eye. It\u2019s activated by meditating for a scene in a place of power that the Claimant has successfully put under their aegis. Reach is spent on Advanced Duration. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not only is the King able to see every physical aspect of his realm, but he is also able to sense the Supernal energies flowing through it. This acts as Sacred Geometry, subtly drawing the Claimant\u2019s attention to ley lines and nodes within sensory range. Like the spell adding Death or Spirit and potentially other arcana alerts the Claimant to other sources of arcane power to cultivate and command. This attainment may be activated within the same scene that the primary attainment is activated and the Reach is spent on Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second: All Within is Known to Me.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Politics 3, Space 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this attainment the King is finely attuned to the subjects upon which their Nimbus lays. Whenever the subject of their Nimbus would be subject to something that would trigger the King\u2019s Peripheral Mage Sight the King\u2019s Peripheral Mage Sight is made aware of it, and of the subject that was acted upon. This effect is activated on a subject as an Instant Action after the Claimant lays their Nimbus on it, and has Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The King benefits from Pierce Deception with regards to the subjects they have laid their Nimbus on. In addition to being able to discern lies or deception from their subjects, this also affords the Claimant a CoW against Veiling or other supernaturally covert effects on their subjects that their Peripheral Mage Sight might normally not react to. This is activated as an Instant Action on a subject after the Claimant lays their Nimbus on it, and has Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third: I Am One With the Land</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Space 3. In addition to the Politics 3 requirement of the previous attainment, the Claimant must increase the other Skill they used to meet the requirements of the legacy to 3, or must attain two dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After a scene of meaningful interaction with one of their subjects the King may upgrade the Sympathetic Strength of their connection to a subject of their Nimbus to Strong. The other Reach is spent on Advanced Duration. This has side effects, making it difficult for the subject to ignore or be out of reach of their King, but also can color the King\u2019s Nimbus, effects of the Long Term Nimbus will likely strike the subjects first if at all possible, and the King may suffer adverse effects if they neglect their subjects or allow them to suffer as their Nimbus rebounds on them and reminds them of the responsibilities they have assumed. It\u2019s possible to maintain a number of these strengthened connections equal to the King\u2019s dots in Space at Advanced Scale, though other Strong connections may be held if they occur naturally. If the King wishes to replace one Strong connection with another they may do so by activating this attainment again.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The King may make his claims upon his subjects explicit to anyone with sight to see. He may as an Instant Action and with Advanced Duration place Invisible Runes upon the subject regardless of whether or not the subject is within Sensory Range, or the strength of their Sympathetic Connection, though this does still require a Sympathetic Yantra. Not only do these runes declare the will of the King, but they may be used as a Runes Yantra for the purposes of performing magic on the subject.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fourth: The Land Protects Me as I Protect It</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Space 4, Politics 4, and the other skill requirements of the previous attainment.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This attainment mimics Perfect Sympathy. The King receives 8-again on any mundane roll to affect one of the subjects of their Nimbus that is also subject to the previous attainment or otherwise at Strong either to influence, observe, or guess what will happen in the event of interactions. In addition the Sympathy is so close that the Claimant may choose to enact a Clash of Wills on any Sympathetic magic targeted at them or one of these subjects and if they win they may redirect it to one of their subjects instead. Or if they choose they may redirect Sympathetic magic to themselves, or to one of the other subjects of this attainment. This attainment is activated by a scene of meaningful interaction with a subject of the previous attainment and has Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Resonance, Ley Lines and Nodes that reside in an area controlled by the Claimant\u2019s touch of their Nimbus, and that has a Sympathetic Connection of Strong become freely manipulable by them. As an Instant Action and with Advanced Duration they can change any of these features, if they are not within Sensory Range they may do so if they possess a Sympathetic Yantra. This can even allow them to cause the energies of far flung places separated by any distance to come together and interact. This frequently creates Mysteries with strange and difficult to predict results, new Hallows, or other places of power. Though the main part of the attainment can help with determining how it will play out there have been stories of the Supernal energies of places being altered to disastrous effect for the King from accidentally unleashing a Bound that uses the flux of power to hunt them down, or a plague that strikes the King no matter where they are or other things left to the ST to decide. The King and their subjects are as close to mystical union as possible and the effects that the subjects suffer may well come back on the King\u2019s own head.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth: The World is Mine</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisities: Space 5, in addition to the Politics 4 requirement from the previous attainment, the Claimant must increase the other skill they used to meet the requirements to 4, or must attain a third dot in a second skill from the list of requirements, or two dots in a third skill in the list.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As an Instant Action and with Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale of subjects so long as the Claimant has a Sympathetic Yantra and a Strong Connection corresponding to each the King may cause themselves to be Co-Located with any of the subjects of their Nimbus. This allows them to benefit from any of the benefits or drawbacks that these subjects of their power bring with them simultaneously. They may move freely between their subjects as an Instant Action or as an Instant Action cause features of their subjects to move from one to the other such as a Hallow being placed in a Verge halfway across the world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With such an acute understanding and control of the subjects under their domain the King finds it much easier to draw the Supernal directly to the Fallen in the climax of their power. They may, at the STs discretion, reduce the number of rolls to summon a Supernal Being by their Gnosis when in a territory marked by their Nimbus, and these roll requirements may be reduced further by the alignment of energies or features they have brought together via the use of their previous attainments. If they bring the required number of rolls to 0 they automatically succeed at summoning the entity after 1 ritual scene with no risk of the Abyss leaking in, though the entity must still leave at the end of its time or risk being consumed by the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Edited for format.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-22-2019, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T11:26:53-08:00","id":1350269,"title":"","content":"Is this the topic you were looking for ? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278930-and-now-for-something-different\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...hing-different</a><br /> <br /> They embody the True King archetype well, granting protection to their subjects, investing authority or demonstrating favor via the royal seal, coming to their aid, being duty bound to help, knowing the secrets of their land and reshaping it as they see fit.<br /> <br /> I wish there was a Fisher King type effect between them and the land. It happens between them and their subjects via the sympathetic redirection, but not between King and Kingdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-22-2019, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T12:06:46-08:00","id":1350281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1350259-the-tellurians-an-update?p=1350269#post1350269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish there was a Fisher King type effect between them and the land. It happens between them and their subjects via the sympathetic redirection, but not between King and Kingdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that\u2019s the one. Thank you!<br /> <br /> As for what I\u2019ve quoted from you, take note, the Nimbus can be put on Places, and thus counts as a subject. Thus they absolutely have a Fisher King connection with their realm(s). If the land fares poorly then the way Sympathy works it should have an adverse effect on the Tellurian. This should be particularly true at the 4th attainment. I just didn\u2019t quantify it in mechanics in order to give the ST creative discretion in leveraging that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T13:17:59-08:00","id":1350295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1350259-the-tellurians-an-update#post1350259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I started a topic similar to this some time ago, but I can't find it, and there was never a final written form. So here it is now. It should be noted that this legacy takes advantage of a quirk in the Nimbus rules which never makes it explicit how large an area can be marked by the Nimbus to get around considerations of AoE Scale. Still, I would recommend that if your player tries to claim that the world is a place, or something similar, that you blap them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow a player to claim the world if they could figure out how to meaningfully interact with the entire planet all at once; I'd also make them defend their claim.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not only is the King able to see every physical aspect of his realm, but he is also able to sense the Supernal energies flowing through it. This acts as Sacred Geometry, subtly drawing the Claimant\u2019s attention to ley lines and nodes within sensory range. Like the spell adding Death or Spirit and potentially other arcana alerts the Claimant to other sources of arcane power to cultivate and command. This attainment may be activated within the same scene that the primary attainment is activated and the Reach is spent on Advanced Duration.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>This should just require Prime 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second: All Within is Known to Me.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Politics 3, Space 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this attainment the King is finely attuned to the subjects upon which their Nimbus lays. Whenever the subject of their Nimbus would be subject to something that would trigger the King\u2019s Peripheral Mage Sight the King\u2019s Peripheral Mage Sight is made aware of it, and of the subject that was acted upon. This effect is activated on a subject as an Instant Action after the Claimant lays their Nimbus on it, and has Advanced Duration.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I like this attainment, but don't think the &quot;instant action&quot; and &quot;advanced duration&quot; clauses are necessary, it should take effect and last for as long as the nimbus is on the subject (since this requires regular maintenance).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The King benefits from Pierce Deception with regards to the subjects they have laid their Nimbus on. In addition to being able to discern lies or deception from their subjects, this also affords the Claimant a CoW against Veiling or other supernaturally covert effects on their subjects that their Peripheral Mage Sight might normally not react to. This is activated as an Instant Action on a subject after the Claimant lays their Nimbus on it, and has Advanced Duration.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>There's no need for Instant Casting, the Mage is the beneficiary of <i>Pierce Deception</i>, I'd have the other reach be the one that grants a symbolic representation of the actual truth.<br /> <br /> [quote]<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third: I Am One With the Land</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Space 3. In addition to the Politics 3 requirement of the previous attainment, the Claimant must increase the other Skill they used to meet the requirements of the legacy to 3, or must attain two dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After a scene of meaningful interaction with one of their subjects the King may upgrade the Sympathetic Strength of their connection to a subject of their Nimbus to Strong. The other Reach is spent on Advanced Duration. This has side effects, making it difficult for the subject to ignore or be out of reach of their King, but also can color the King\u2019s Nimbus, effects of the Long Term Nimbus will likely strike the subjects first if at all possible, and the King may suffer adverse effects if they neglect their subjects or allow them to suffer as their Nimbus rebounds on them and reminds them of the responsibilities they have assumed. It\u2019s possible to maintain a number of these strengthened connections equal to the King\u2019s dots in Space at Advanced Scale, though other Strong connections may be held if they occur naturally. If the King wishes to replace one Strong connection with another they may do so by activating this attainment again.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Considering the amount of work required to maintain the connections and the potential detriment to having too many, I wouldn't limit the number they can have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The King may make his claims upon his subjects explicit to anyone with sight to see. He may as an Instant Action and with Advanced Duration place Invisible Runes upon the subject regardless of whether or not the subject is within Sensory Range, or the strength of their Sympathetic Connection, though this does still require a Sympathetic Yantra. Not only do these runes declare the will of the King, but they may be used as a Runes Yantra for the purposes of performing magic on the subject.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fourth: The Land Protects Me as I Protect It</span></span><br /> ...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Resonance, Ley Lines and Nodes that reside in an area controlled by the Claimant\u2019s touch of their Nimbus, and that has a Sympathetic Connection of Strong become freely manipulable by them. As an Instant Action and with Advanced Duration they can change any of these features, if they are not within Sensory Range they may do so if they possess a Sympathetic Yantra. This can even allow them to cause the energies of far flung places separated by any distance to come together and interact. This frequently creates Mysteries with strange and difficult to predict results, new Hallows, or other places of power. Though the main part of the attainment can help with determining how it will play out there have been stories of the Supernal energies of places being altered to disastrous effect for the King from accidentally unleashing a Bound that uses the flux of power to hunt them down, or a plague that strikes the King no matter where they are or other things left to the ST to decide. The King and their subjects are as close to mystical union as possible and the effects that the subjects suffer may well come back on the King\u2019s own head.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth: The World is Mine</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisities: Space 5, in addition to the Politics 4 requirement from the previous attainment, the Claimant must increase the other skill they used to meet the requirements to 4, or must attain a third dot in a second skill from the list of requirements, or two dots in a third skill in the list.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As an Instant Action and with Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale of subjects so long as the Claimant has a Sympathetic Yantra and a Strong Connection corresponding to each the King may cause themselves to be Co-Located with any of the subjects of their Nimbus. This allows them to benefit from any of the benefits or drawbacks that these subjects of their power bring with them simultaneously. They may move freely between their subjects as an Instant Action or as an Instant Action cause features of their subjects to move from one to the other such as a Hallow being placed in a Verge halfway across the world.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could be wrong, but I believe the Claimant themself would count as a Sympathetic Yantra equal to their connection for all of these attainments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Prime 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With such an acute understanding and control of the subjects under their domain the King finds it much easier to draw the Supernal directly to the Fallen in the climax of their power. They may, at the STs discretion, reduce the number of rolls to summon a Supernal Being by their Gnosis when in a territory marked by their Nimbus, and these roll requirements may be reduced further by the alignment of energies or features they have brought together via the use of their previous attainments. If they bring the required number of rolls to 0 they automatically succeed at summoning the entity after 1 ritual scene with no risk of the Abyss leaking in, though the entity must still leave at the end of its time or risk being consumed by the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Edited for format.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I like it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall I really like this update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T15:32:38-08:00","id":1350327,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=proindrakenzol;n1350295]<br /> I'd allow a player to claim the world if they could figure out how to meaningfully interact with the entire planet all at once; I'd also make them defend their claim.<br /> <br /> This should just require Prime 1.<br /> <br /> I like this attainment, but don't think the &amp;quot;instant action&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;advanced duration&amp;quot; clauses are necessary, it should take effect and last for as long as the nimbus is on the subject (since this requires regular maintenance).<br /> <br /> There's no need for Instant Casting, the Mage is the beneficiary of <i>Pierce Deception</i>, I'd have the other reach be the one that grants a symbolic representation of the actual truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third: I Am One With the Land</span></span><br /> <br /> Considering the amount of work required to maintain the connections and the potential detriment to having too many, I wouldn't limit the number they can have.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong, but I believe the Claimant themself would count as a Sympathetic Yantra equal to their connection for all of these attainments.<br /> <br /> I like it.<br /> <br /> Overall I really like this update. </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> Good point, yeet the Exarchs if you can!<br /> <br /> Good catch on the first Prime Optional. I\u2019ll fix that first chance I get. I forgot that the Optional can start at an arcana rating of one.<br /> <br /> Mmm, it\u2019s not really modeled off of a spell, but I thought maybe an action cost to modify your Nimbus to send info back to you might be called for. The Prime Optional makes an additional modification to your Nimbus when it\u2019s on something. I\u2019ll consider your suggestions though.<br /> <br /> I did consider just making the number of subjects unlimited. Nimbus placement can be maintained by placed spells or just slapping it down, but yeah it would require maintenance. I\u2019ll probably change that.<br /> <br /> Hmm, it\u2019s possible the Claimant may count as the Yantra considering how tightly his Sympathy gets bound up, but I kind of like the idea of carrying tokens of your Sympathies with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}